tting is an experience that  always keeps you guessing sometimes it's  moments like is this excursion into a  cave going to be worthwhile  while other times you might find  yourself stranded out at sea because you  rented a room in the wrong hotel  don't get me wrong skyrim has moments  like this too but oblivion surprised me  in ways skyrim never managed to  maybe it's because todd yes i was in the  chess club howard and the team at  bethesda  were still experimenting with their  flagship rpg series or maybe the team  itself looked  very different back then but oblivion  just had an ambitious innocence to it  that led to some  wonderfully memorable moments in a  seemingly familiar  world sure a lot of my passion for  oblivion is fueled by an ambiguous  intangible sense of nostalgia like  stepping out of the prison sewers for  the first time or hearing the music  swell as you explore the green hills of  the heartlands or your first encounter  with a dark brotherhood but i think  even today it's worth giving oblivion a  shot for the many stories it holds  and because it will probably be another  half decade before we hear more about  the elder scrolls 6.  anyway what are some of your favorite  memories in oblivion let me know in the  comments below  and as always thank you so much for  watching  by azura by azura by astoria it's the  grand  champion i can't believe it's you  standing  here next to me  [Music]  you
 

